{
  "id": "ss.char.prism",
  "name": "Prism",
  "description": "The cicada of the eight, and the loud one. Pink hair cut to a point on top — the diamond it used to be — with two pointed pigtails sticking straight out to the sides, both eyes shut in two happy arcs, and the mouth open round: Prism is singing. What comes out is the chirp, a hum thrown outward in a ring, and the ring is drawn leaving the mouth in the idle, faint and cold, because it is a sound and not a scent. Two long clear wings lie folded down the back from the shoulders, and the dress has the facet — one plane lit, one in shade, a ridge between. Long light legs, because this is also the one that runs, and the feelers held the widest apart on the roster, one thrown forward and one back: the survivor that finds things. Same dead organ as the rest, worn as a brooch. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
